I've been thinking about the polypiling problem.  I usually don't
polypile, not because I have some sort of moral abhorance, but rather
that I don't like to spend all that time racing up and down the stairs
gathering junk together for the pile.  But I can see where some people
would think that it unbalances the game.  Well, why not introduce a new
mode to the game?  We have explore and normal game modes, why not a
demigod mode or some such?  In demigod mode a polymorph wand would only
affect items that are or were living at one time, i.e. food items,
creatures and corpses.  Thereby you could still get those certain armor
items with a WoP, but you could really polypile with any useful
results.  One could also eliminate rings of conflict from the game, and
maybe other items that people feel make it too easy to win.  The whole
idea being that in demigod mode, the player had better know an awful lot 
more about the game than jsust how to pile things together, zap a wand
and suddenly be ready to head for the wizard.  Of course demigod mode
winners would have their own high score list so that they could show
off thier talent to other nethack addicts.

Just some thoughts...

Charles


